[Event "Queen's Gambit vs QGD"]

{2.c4 attacks d5 from the side. Against the Declined White aims for Bg5, e3 and either a minority attack or central play.}
1. d4 {[%csl Ge5,Gc5] White claims the centre and opens the c1-bishop. c4 next is the Queen's Gambit.}
1... d5 {Black stakes the centre. White's c4 next offers the Queen's Gambit.}
2. c4 {[%cal Gc4d5] The Queen's Gambit: c4 trades a wing pawn for a centre pawn.}
2... e6 {The QGD: rock solid, but the c8-bishop is locked in.}
3. Nc3 {Adds pressure on d5. Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
3... Nf6 {Defends d5. Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.}
4. Bg5 {[%cal Gg5f6] Pins the defender of d5. Develops the bishop to g5, where it controls f4 and eyes the knight on f6. Black's last move put a knight on f6, which this now pressures.}
4... Be7 {Breaks the pin. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
 (4... Nbd7 {Hides the Elephant Trap. Develops the knight to d7, where it controls e5.}
5. cxd5 {Exchange. Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
5... exd5 {Black recaptures with the pawn, entering the Exchange structure. White's minority attack with b4–b5 is the main plan.}
6. e3 {Do not take d5: 6.Nxd5?? Nxd5 7.Bxd8 Bb4+ loses a piece.}
6... c6 {Black supports d5 and controls b5 and d5. White's Bd3 next.}
7. Bd3 {White develops and controls e4.}
)
5. e3 {White supports d4 and opens the f1-bishop.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6. Nf3 {White develops toward e5. Black's ...h6 next asks the bishop a question.}
6... h6 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on h6 eyes the bishop on g5.}
7. Bh4 {Keeps the pin. Moves the bishop out of attack to h4.}
7... b6 {The Tartakower: the bishop goes to b7. The pawn on b6 controls a5 and c5.}
8. Be2 {Quiet and solid. The bishop backs up the f3-knight (no annoying ...Bg4 pin pressure) and White is one move from castling.}
8... Bb7 {Develops on the long diagonal. Fianchettoes the bishop on b7, where it rakes the long diagonal through c6 and d5.}
9. Bxf6 {Trades to weaken d5. Takes the knight on f6; Black will want to recapture.}
9... Bxf6 {Black recaptures with the bishop. Black gets the bishop pair but White's centre is solid.}
10. cxd5 {Opens the c-file. Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
10... exd5 {Black recaptures with the pawn. Black has a solid centre; White's plan: O-O and b4.}
11. b4 {[%cal Gb4b5] A minority attack. Gains space on the queenside; the pawn on b4 takes a5 and c5 away from the opponent.} *

[Event "Queen's Gambit Exchange"]

{The Exchange gives the Carlsbad structure: a minority attack on the queenside.}
1. d4 {White claims the centre and opens the c1-bishop. c4 next is the Queen's Gambit.}
1... d5 {Black stakes the centre. White's c4 next offers the Queen's Gambit.}
2. c4 {Queen's Gambit. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
2... e6 {QGD. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
3. Nc3 {Pressure. Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
3... Nf6 {Black develops and covers e4. White's Bg5 or cxd5 next.}
4. cxd5 {The Exchange. Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
4... exd5 {Black recaptures with the pawn. White's minority attack with b4–b5 is the main plan.}
5. Bg5 {Pins. Develops the bishop to g5, where it controls f4 and eyes the knight on f6.}
5... c6 {Black supports d5 and controls b5. White's Qc2 next.}
6. Qc2 {[%cal Gc2h7] Stops ...Bf5 ideas and eyes h7. The queen goes to c2 and controls e4.}
6... Be7 {A modest but safe home for the bishop: it shields the f6-knight from pins and lets Black castle next. Don't worry that it looks passive; it can reroute later.}
7. e3 {White supports d4 and opens the f1-bishop. Bd3 and Nge2 next.}
7... Nbd7 {Black develops and supports ...Nf8 or ...Ne4. White's plan: Bd3 and O-O.}
8. Bd3 {[%cal Gd3h7] Develops toward the kingside. The bishop on d3 controls e4.}
8... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9. Nge2 {A flexible setup that allows f3 and e4. That clears the way to castle kingside.} *

[Event "Queen's Gambit Accepted"]

{After 2...dxc4 White simply recovers the pawn with e3 and Bxc4.}
1. d4 {White claims the centre and opens the c1-bishop.}
1... d5 {Black stakes the centre. White's c4 next offers the Queen's Gambit.}
2. c4 {Queen's Gambit. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
2... dxc4 {Accepts, giving up the centre. Takes the pawn on c4, and it cannot be taken back at once.}
3. Nf3 {Stops ...e5. Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
3... Nf6 {Black develops and covers e4. White's e3 next to regain the pawn.}
4. e3 {Opens the bishop to take c4. Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 controls f4 and supports the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the bishop on f1.}
4... e6 {Black supports d5 and opens the f8-bishop. White's Bxc4 next.}
5. Bxc4 {Regains the pawn. Takes the pawn on c4, and it cannot be taken back at once.}
5... c5 {Hits d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... a6 {Prepares ...b5. The pawn on a6 controls b5.}
7. a4 {[%cal Ga4b5] Stops ...b5. Gains space on the queenside; the pawn on a4 takes b5 away from the opponent.} *

[Event "Queen's Gambit vs Slav, Albin & Chigorin"]

{Other replies to 2.c4: the Slav, the Albin Countergambit and the Chigorin.}
1. d4 {White claims the centre and opens the c1-bishop.}
1... d5 {Black stakes the centre. White's c4 next offers the Queen's Gambit.}
2. c4 {Queen's Gambit. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
2... c6 {The Slav. Supports the centre: the pawn on c6 controls b5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
 (2... e5 {The Albin Countergambit. Claims the centre: the pawn on e5 controls f4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
3. dxe5 {White takes the pawn. Black's ...d4 next gains space.}
3... d4 {Gains space. Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c3 and e3.}
4. Nf3 {White develops toward e5. Black's ...Nc6 next.}
4... Nc6 {Black develops and pressures e5. White's g3 next.}
5. g3 {The bishop goes to g2. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
)
 (2... Nc6 {The Chigorin. Develops the knight to c6, where it controls e5 and eyes the pawn on d4.}
3. Nf3 {White develops toward e5. Black's ...Bg4 next.}
3... Bg4 {Pins. Develops the bishop to g4, where it controls f5 and e6. White's last move put a knight on f3, which this now pressures.}
4. cxd5 {White takes the pawn. Black's ...Bxf3 next.}
4... Bxf3 {Black takes the knight. White recaptures with the g-pawn.}
5. gxf3 {White recaptures. White has the bishop pair and an open g-file.}
5... Qxd5 {Black takes the pawn.}
6. e3 {Solid; White has the bishop pair. Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 controls f4 and supports the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the bishop on f1.}
)
3. Nf3 {White develops toward e5. Black's ...Nf6 next.}
3... Nf6 {Black develops and covers e4. White's Nc3 next.}
4. Nc3 {White develops and supports e4. Black's ...dxc4 next.}
4... dxc4 {Black takes the pawn.}
5. a4 {[%cal Ga4b5] Stops ...b5. Gains space on the queenside; the pawn on a4 takes b5 away from the opponent.}
5... Bf5 {Develops outside the chain. The bishop on f5 controls e4.}
6. e3 {Prepares Bxc4. Supports the centre: the pawn on e3 controls f4 and supports the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the bishop on f1.}
6... e6 {Black supports d5 and opens the f8-bishop. White's Bxc4 next.}
7. Bxc4 {Regains the pawn. Takes the pawn on c4, and it cannot be taken back at once.}
7... Bb4 {Pins the knight. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
8. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.} *
